{"step_index":2136,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-03T08:45:43Z","input_tokens":2907,"cache_read_tokens":99211,"output_tokens":2321,"content":"The refactor has been implemented, tested, and verified. Here is a summary of the changes:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Tab 1 Clean-Up: Focused Invoice Math Audit\nIn [`components/AuditScorecard.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/AuditScorecard.js):\n- **Removed the dark inline card:** Completely removed the *\"Tax & ITR Insights Sec 44AD Presumptive\"* box, the 3 insight pills, the inline digital receipts slider, and the Gemini advisory callout from Tab 1.\n- **Dedicated Layout:** Tab 1 now focuses strictly on:\n  1. Live Tax Invoice Preview (left)\n  2. Audit Verdict & Discrepancy Diff Cards (top right)\n  3. Bill Header Inputs (Supplier Name, GSTIN, Billed Grand Total)\n  4. Item Breakdown & Math Verification Table (Qty $\\times$ Rate, Blurry Flags, Inline Editing)\n  5. GST Tax Rate & Intra/Inter-State Split Controls (Quick preset buttons: 0%, 5%, 12%, 18%, 28%)\n- **New Action Button:** Added `[💾 Save Bill to Tax Ledger]` directly into the action bar alongside `[📋 Copy Note]`, `[📲 WhatsApp]`, `[📑 CA Slip]`, and `[← Back]`.\n- Clicking `[💾 Save Bill to Tax Ledger]` persists the current bill into `localStorage` (`audit_it_tax_ledger_bills`) and shows an instant confirmation toast.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Tab 2 Built: Accumulative Business Tax Ledger & ITR Engine\nIn [`components/TaxAndITRTab.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/TaxAndITRTab.js):\n\n#### A. Stored Invoice Bills Table & Summary Metrics\n- **Summary Cards Bar:**\n  - **Total Bills Verified:** Count of saved bills.\n  - **Total Purchases (COGS):** $\\sum \\text{Subtotals}$ of all stored invoices.\n  - **Total Claimable GST ITC:** $\\sum \\text{Taxes}$ (CGST + SGST + IGST) across all stored invoices.\n- **Bills Table:** Displays Date, Invoice No., Supplier Name, GSTIN validation tag, Subtotal, CGST, SGST, IGST, Verified Total, and **Actions**:\n  - `[👁️ View]`: Loads the bill directly into Tab 1 for inspection or editing.\n  - `[🗑️]`: Deletes the bill from the ledger.\n- **Empty State Guard:** Allows 1-click addition of the current invoice to start accumulating bills.\n\n#### B. Aggregated GST ITC Ledger (GSTR-3B Preparation)\n- **3 Accumulation Pools:** Separate cards displaying accumulated **CGST Pool**, **SGST Pool**, and **IGST Pool** available to offset monthly output tax liabilities.\n- **Section 16(2) Compliance Alert:** Flags any invoices with missing or invalid GSTIN format and quantifies the tax amount at risk.\n- **Statutory 180-Day Rule Notice:** Reminds shopkeepers to settle vendor dues within 180 days of invoice date to prevent mandatory ITC reversal with 18% penal interest.\n\n#### C. Customizable Annual Business & ITR Calculator (ITR-4 vs ITR-3)\n- **Turnover Input:** Annual retail counter sales input (defaults to ₹30,00,000).\n- **Mode Toggle:**\n  - **Mode 1: Presumptive Section 44AD (ITR-4):**\n    - Digital receipts ratio slider (default 80% digital, 20% cash).\n    - Configurable deemed profit rates (minimum 6% for digital/UPI, 8% for cash).\n    - Deemed Net Business Profit computation.\n  - **Mode 2: Normal Business P&L (ITR-3):**\n    - Cost of Goods Sold (COGS) automatically populated from the ledger's total purchases with a `[⚡ Auto-fill Ledger]` button.\n    - Operating expenses (rent, electricity, salaries) input.\n    - $\\text{Net Profit} = \\text{Turnover} - (\\text{COGS} + \\text{Opex})$.\n- **Live Tax Liability Summary:**\n  - Standard deduction of ₹75,000 auto-applied.\n  - New Tax Regime slab calculation (FY 2025-26 / AY 2026-27).\n  - **Section 87A Rebate:** Automatically identifies when net taxable income $\\le \\text{₹7,00,000}$ and applies **100% Tax Waiver (₹0.00 Tax Payable)**.\n  - **Section 44AB Tax Audit Check:** Evaluates turnover thresholds (₹2 Cr / ₹3 Cr under 44AD, ₹1 Cr / ₹10 Cr under Normal P&L based on digital turnover share).\n\n#### D. Data Management & Export\n- **`[📥 Export Consolidated Tax & ITC (CSV)]`:** Downloads a clean UTF-8 CSV containing the accumulated ledger summary, stored bills list, and ITR computation.\n- **`[🖨️ Print / PDF]`:** Generates a formatted printout for CA review.\n- **`[🗑️ Clear Ledger]`:** Empties the persistent ledger with a safety confirmation prompt.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Application State & Navigation Integration\n- In [`app.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/app.js):\n  - Initialized `this.savedBills` from `localStorage` (seeded with the sample invoice on first run so the ledger is immediately interactive).\n  - Implemented `handleSaveBillToLedger(invoice, audit)` to upsert bills by invoice number or ID.\n  - Wired top navigation tab buttons (`🧾 Invoice Math Audit` and `📊 Tax & ITR Filing`) with live badge counts of stored bills.\n  - Added `openTaxLedger()` and wired dashboard quick access button in [`components/DashboardHero.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/DashboardHero.js).\n- In [`routes/tax_advisory.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/routes/tax_advisory.py) & [`server.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py):\n  - FastAPI `/api/tax/calculate-advisory` endpoint tested and serving live on `http://localhost:3000`.","thinking":"The FastAPI server is confirmed to be running as expected. The task shifts to addressing the user's requirements for Tab 1. The focus is on removing specific UI elements within the audit scorecard component. The removal of the \"Tax & ITR Insights\" section is verified and recorded.\n\n\nCompleted the UI and logic for Tab 1, including the addition of a \"Save Bill to Tax Ledger\" button. This button saves the current verified bill data to local storage and updates the ledger. The focus now shifts to constructing Tab 2, which will function as an accumulative ledger and tax engine.\n\nTab 2's development has begun with the creation of the Stored Invoice Bills table, including all specified columns and a summary bar. The aggregated GST ITC Ledger is also in progress with separate pools for each tax type and statutory compliance checks. Finally, an annual business and ITR calculator is implemented with mode toggles and default inputs.\n\n\n"}
